comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T14:43:01.407Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status searches for test-name-pattern,zero tests,linked-test no-op success,GH-982,and test meaningfulness found pm-m0b7h8 for no-op linked-test mutation and pm-4i73 for meaningfulness,but no item owning zero-execution runner receipts. GitHub issue #1138 is a later recurrence with a distinct execution boundary."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:25.479Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: linked-test execution and connected recovery regressions passed, including zero-run negative controls; full coverage passed 8,099 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:16.706Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: filtered linked-test success now requires a recognized positive runner receipt, so a dot-only reporter cannot certify execution and fails with missing_positive_execution_receipt. Shared structured-entry grammar removes duplicated classifiers; negative controls and exact coverage pass."
  "2026-08-29T04:41:16.228Z","harness:codex","Review-round findings: CodeRabbit identified that pass 0 alone can misclassify a nonempty execution and that missing_positive_execution_receipt is not yet generated into the observable contract. Reopened for count-aware classification and contract parity."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:27.229Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: a regression distinguishes execution count from pass count, the missing-positive-receipt refusal is present in generated SDK/CLI contracts, linked tests passed, all generated surfaces are current, and exact coverage passed 8,111 tests at 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T05:25:27.756Z","harness:codex","A pass count is not an execution count: filtered-run integrity must use explicit executed-test evidence and expose missing positive receipts through the public refusal contract."
